# "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a nonland permanent": with only lands on Bot1's side the Rite cannot be cast, even
# with {W}{B} to pay; an attempted cast targeting Bot2's Mox Jet rolls back. A land is also not a legal target (the refusal naming Bot2's Island). Bot1
# then casts a Mox Pearl, sacrifices it to the Rite (untapped, a cost of its own), and the Rite exiles the Mox Jet.

